  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "One jar file from the REST branch didn't make it into the (3.0B1) trunk.  Without this jar, multipart/mime posts (uploading binary files) fails.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Also, I looked in junit.fedora.test.api.TestRESTAPI.java and found that the testAddDatastream() method only attempts to create an \"X\" datastream by posting some XML.  It doesn't attempt to create an \"M\" datastream by uploading a file.   That's how this error slipped under our radar.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The test method should create both an \"X\" datastream and an \"M\" datastream.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The missing jar file (in SVN Browse):  ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://fedora-commons.svn.sourceforge.net/viewvc/fedora-commons/fedora-rest/trunk/lib/jersey/mail.jar"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://fedora-commons.svn.sourceforge.net/viewvc/fedora-commons/fedora-rest/trunk/lib/jersey/mail.jar",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
