  "description": "<p>One jar file from the REST branch didn't make it into the (3.0B1) trunk.  Without this jar, multipart/mime posts (uploading binary files) fails.</p>\n\n<p>Also, I looked in junit.fedora.test.api.TestRESTAPI.java and found that the testAddDatastream() method only attempts to create an \"X\" datastream by posting some XML.  It doesn't attempt to create an \"M\" datastream by uploading a file.   That's how this error slipped under our radar.</p>\n\n<p>The test method should create both an \"X\" datastream and an \"M\" datastream.</p>\n\n<p>The missing jar file (in SVN Browse):  <a href=\"http://fedora-commons.svn.sourceforge.net/viewvc/fedora-commons/fedora-rest/trunk/lib/jersey/mail.jar\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://fedora-commons.svn.sourceforge.net/viewvc/fedora-commons/fedora-rest/trunk/lib/jersey/mail.jar</a></p>",
